# Detailed guide

Start with the outcome, the supported baseline and the prerequisites, then give the steps in the order people must perform them. Use a detailed guide for a task that needs substantial, maintained instructions. The shared limits for every page template are on [Page templates](index.html).

## When to use it

Use it to install the companion, upgrade a supported version or recover a known configuration. Put a check at each point where a mistake would otherwise go unnoticed. If the subject splits into independent tasks, use a [guide](guide.html).

## Structure and behaviour

Include a contents list, meaningful headings, short code blocks where needed and verified recovery information ([WG-050](../../content/writing-guidelines/clear-structure.html#wg-050), [WG-051](../../content/writing-guidelines/clear-structure.html#wg-051)). Publish a real first-publication date and keep dated change notes that describe what a reader will notice ([WG-091](../../content/writing-guidelines/change-notes.html#wg-091)). In current publishing metadata, page history belongs to `page_history`. Do not build new guidance around the removed published-dates component. See [Publishing source history](../source-history.html).

## Home Assistant boundary

The guide is instructional content, not an installer. Reading a step does not complete it. Do not invent a supported Home Assistant version, release URL or backup location. Keep credentials and private household details out of public examples.

